OASIS 0008 -- Coyote: the TOE's receive ring in card memory, wired into the shell.
Working-tree change to parcore/libstf/coyote (expected HEAD b21b4ec6), made 2026-10-11 (toe-buffer
WP2). Inert unless TCP_STACK_RX_DDR_BYPASS_EN = 0 (oasis: ENABLE_HTTP_TOE_BUFFER / --toe-buffer):
  - hw/hdl/network/tcp/tcp_mem_mux.sv: new, merges tcp_stack's two memory channels (tx, rx) onto the
    one exported TCP memory channel; rx addresses get bit 29; tx writes store-and-forward.
  - hw/hdl/network/stack/network_stack.sv: under `ifdef EN_TCP_RX_DDR, tcp_stack #(.RX_DDR_BYPASS_EN(0))
    + tcp_mem_mux; otherwise the original text.
  - cmake/FindCoyoteHW.cmake, scripts/base.tcl.in, hw/templates/common/lynx_pkg_tmplt.txt: the CMake
    variable that writes RX_DDR_BYPASS into the TOE's HLS config also emits EN_TCP_RX_DDR (only when 0),
    and must be the literal 0 or 1.
Apply with hardware/patches/apply.sh (or: git -C parcore/libstf/coyote apply <this file>).
See hardware/patches/README.md, "The receive ring wired into the shell (0008)".

